pr: r2
title: JVM: Rakudo on newdisp -- scaffolding, the flip, semantics parity
branch: pr/02-rakudo-on-newdisp

# Sections R2 + R3 + R4 (R4 without its last commit, which opens r3):
# log lines 12..73, 62 commits. 17 groups.
#
# Moves in this file are all file-disjoint (checked with git show --stat):
#  - the five watched-runner commits touch only tools/build/run-watched.raku
#    and tools/build/watched-run.raku, which nothing else in 12..73 touches;
#  - the R2 frontend fixes / runtime-and-runner split swaps two docs-free
#    runs whose files do not overlap (see the per-group notes);
#  - in R4 the diagnostics, op-gap and native groups are gathered across
#    each other where the stats prove the files disjoint.
# The revert pair a691c24c81 / 99faeae96d is inside one group and nets to
# nothing.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- R2

= keep
- 195d01488c Let the JVM use the ignorecase/ignoremark string ops

= Add a watched runner for long builds and test sweeps
tools/build/watched-run.raku runs a command tee'd to a log, gives up on a
silence longer than --stall or a total longer than --max (SIGINT, SIGTERM,
SIGKILL in turn so the child's own JVMs unwind first), echoes --show
matches with elapsed seconds, and in -t mode runs many test files --jobs
at a time, each under its own watchdog and log. All timing lives in one
react block. run-watched.raku is the first cut it grew out of.
# moved: ebe919924e, ef861a191f, 9f57d0e888 and 78a2844993 pulled earlier
# to sit with b24c0cc3b1 -- all five touch only the two runner scripts,
# which no other commit in lines 12..73 touches.
- b24c0cc3b1 Add a watched runner for long builds and test runs
- ebe919924e run-watched: move all timing into a react block, add --show
- ef861a191f run-watched: compile --show patterns before the child starts
- 9f57d0e888 run-watched: parallel -t mode for running many test files
- 78a2844993 Add a watched runner for long builds and test sweeps

= RakuAST: give the new-dispatch sites non-moar branches
The seven QAST::Op dispatch emissions get a non-moar branch in the shapes
the legacy frontend already used: onlystar bodies consult the dispatch
cache, private and qualified calls go through Mu's dispatch:<!> and
dispatch:<::>, coercions call the metaobject, .? and smartmatch fall back
to the general path. Routines claim $*DISPATCHER with takedispatcher so
callsame works, dispatch:<...> names arrive as Str literals, and
arguments bind through the runtime binder (custom-args on jvm).
- 3cc89d0f99 RakuAST: give the new-dispatch sites non-moar branches
- f76b11cbee RakuAST/JVM: bind arguments with the runtime binder
- bddeaa5bb0 RakuAST: make the non-moar onlystar proto dispatch work
- cda8ffba3c RakuAST: set up dispatch on backends without new-dispatch

= RakuAST: six frontend fixes the JVM's CORE.c build surfaced
ScopePhaser's typed attributes are tested with isconcrete, not boolified
(a Bool type object's Bool method recursed during the setting build); a
routine whose compilation calls itself is named in the error; chars vs
codes above the BMP and a heredoc stopper passed as a native str;
@!compstuff is not indexed after a fixup drained it; begin-time failures
are rethrown under RAKUDO_DEBUG_TRAIT while a setting builds; and the
code ref table holds one slot per cuid.
