- db5b936249 RakuAST: don't boolify ScopePhaser's typed attributes
- 1ae3324f13 RakuAST: name a routine whose compilation calls it
- 19e815b429 RakuAST: two UTF-16 assumptions that only bite on JVM
- 818e483432 RakuAST: don't index an @!compstuff an earlier fixup drained
- 15334af85c RakuAST/JVM: make begin-time failures visible while building a setting
- 576cea15e0 RakuAST: one code ref table slot per cuid

= JVM: p6sink into the runtime; Proc::Async, runner stack and flags
p6sink yields the sinkee as MoarVM's does and moves out of line into
RakOps (the inline can/callmethod pair cost one indy site per sunk
statement, over the per-class ceiling on its own). A merged Proc::Async
stream ends after one report. The runners give the compiler a 64MB
stack and stop passing -noverify. The Kotlin layer's locals are
camelCase.
# moved: 4c8d35bbc9, 426bb5105c and 1d59200288 pulled earlier over
# 1f193e0e0c, 043778969c and 19ad97bd79 -- Proc/Async.rakumod,
# create-jvm-runner.pl, Binder.kt/RakudoJavaInterop.kt against
# var-lowering.rakumod and code.rakumod.
- 8e9d43fe90 JVM: p6sink yields the sinkee, and moves into the runtime
- ece6ad4897 JVM runners: give the compiler a 64MB stack
- 4c8d35bbc9 JVM: a merged Proc::Async stream ends after one report
- 426bb5105c JVM runners: stop passing -noverify
- 1d59200288 JVM: camelCase the Kotlin variables

= RakuAST: three lowering fixes for frames the runtime binder binds
A for body's frame is not lowered when its code has custom-args (the
binder binds the lexical, the body read the local); an onlystar proto
returns its candidate's result raw on non-moar backends, container and
all; a block thunk's topic parameter carries a type, since the binder
reads the Parameter rather than lowered QAST.
- 1f193e0e0c RakuAST: don't lower in a frame whose signature needs the binder
- 043778969c RakuAST: an onlystar proto returns its candidate's result raw
- 19ad97bd79 RakuAST: give a block thunk's topic parameter a type

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- R3

= Build the newdisp dispatchers on the JVM; assign and rv-decont use them
src/vm/moar/dispatchers.nqp joins the JVM bootstrap, and the first gates
flip: p6attrinited dispatches to raku-is-attr-inited, p6assign to
raku-assign, p6decontrv_internal to raku-rv-decont (with p6box and the
language-revision child the desugar reads). 99-misc.t asks a Parameter
for its .raku.
- a0605f0d7e Build the newdisp dispatchers on the JVM backend too
- ce21534b38 Ask a Parameter for its .raku, not its .perl
- a4753e926e Assign through the raku-assign dispatcher on the JVM too
- 11082bb9fc Decont return values through the raku-rv-decont dispatcher on the JVM too

= JVM: lower parameters again; a failed bind reads in Raku's terms
The lowered form now reproduces the binder's semantics on the JVM, so
custom-args is no longer unconditional there and lex-to-local lowering
works at all. A failed lowered-parameter check raises through a
bind_error handler (p6bindfailerror re-runs the JVM binder over the
frame) instead of "Bind check failed", and a parameter with two names
goes to the full binder. qast-deep-has-op stops at non-QAST leaves.
# The revert pair a691c24c81 / 99faeae96d nets to nothing here: the
# container-vivification fix moved to the nqp side.
- 64b319ee2c Stop qast-deep-has-op recursing into non-QAST leaves
- a691c24c81 RakuAST: don't vivify a container for a lowered parameter's local
- 7db19cba51 JVM: report a failed parameter bind in Raku's terms
- 99faeae96d Revert "RakuAST: don't vivify a container for a lowered parameter's local"
- 7b918f0d2f JVM: bind an aliased named parameter with the full binder
- 94b5dea8e0 RakuAST/JVM: lower parameters instead of always using the binder

= Coerce via raku-coercion and register Raku's HLL dispatchers on the JVM
Both coercion sites of a lowered parameter dispatch on every backend but
js, and the Raku HLL config names raku-call, raku-meth-call,
raku-find-meth, raku-resume-error, raku-hllize, nqp-istype and
raku-isinvokable on the JVM too -- what lang-call and lang-meth-call
hand a Raku object to.
- 6b2af8051c Coerce a parameter through the raku-coercion dispatcher on the JVM too
- f4e594325e Register Raku's HLL dispatchers on the JVM too

= keep
- 5c343f58f0 JVM: flip the remaining dispatch gates; everything now runs on newdisp

= JVM: after the flip -- shared wrap, no Mu catch-all, hllized versions
Routine's newdisp Wrapped role is keyed on js like the dispatchers, so
.wrap works on the JVM; the legacy catch-all invocation handler on Mu is
js-only (raku-invoke does its job, and isinvokable stops answering true
for every object); the version strings handed to Version.new are
hllized so 'use v6.*' works.
# moved: dda808f794 pulled earlier over 3a4ea7c227 -- Raku/Actions.nqp
# against atomicops.rakumod.
- 7a60dd7af4 Share the newdisp wrap implementation with the JVM
- 33e97a5d43 JVM: drop the catch-all invocation handler on Mu
- dda808f794 RakuAST: hllize the version strings handed to Version.new

= Enable atomicint and the integer atomics on the JVM
nqp-jvm implements the integer atomic op family, so the fence around
atomicint and its operators comes down, and the corekeys, settingkeys
and implementation-detail tests drop their jvm-NYI entries for them.
# moved: e551af5e81 pulled earlier over f1d9fb892c, 47d6ae007c and
# d7ca3aa758 -- t/02-rakudo/07-implementation-detail-*.t against
# moar/dispatchers.nqp, Binder.kt/RakOps.kt and BOOTSTRAP.nqp.
- 3a4ea7c227 Enable atomicint and the integer atomics on the JVM
- 88688aaaa7 Graduate the integer atomics off the corekeys jvm-NYI lists
- e551af5e81 Graduate the integer atomics off the implementation-detail jvm lists

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- R4

= RakuAST/JVM: generic coercions and returns resolved per call
raku-coercion delegates a still-generic coercion type to a closure that
instantiates it against the calling frame; the JVM binder instantiates
the is-copy descriptor, passes archetypes its type, and checks a generic
return that instantiates to a native against its box; the nqp binder's
coercive branch instantiates a generic parameter type too.
- f1d9fb892c RakuAST: resolve a generic coercion type per call in raku-coercion
- 47d6ae007c JVM: teach the binder and return check about generics properly
- d7ca3aa758 Instantiate a generic coercion in the nqp binder's coercive branch

= JVM: backtraces, continuations, interop and error reporting at parity
p6staticouter answers null for a mainline (backtraces render again); a
worker resumes a suspended task through continuationreset so a second
suspension finds its prompt; marshalled interop arrays are cast to their
real type; method_not_found_error is installed for the JVM; a constraint
failure says whether the parameter was omitted; a compose failure is
filed like every other backend; RAKUDO_DEBUG_STUB traces stubbing.
