= RakuAST/JVM: native returns stay native; sized natives bound at width
A native-returning routine's inline info drops both the return typecheck
and the decont wrapper, so spliced code stays natively typed end to end
(infix:<+> on ints compiles to add_i again); the binder narrows a sized
native to its declared width.
- b0a2bed850 RakuAST: record native-returning inline info without the return typecheck
- 59f7bde15b RakuAST: a native return's wrappers stay out of its inline info
- ae81fcbae6 JVM: narrow a sized native to its width when the binder binds it

